- (i In case traction power is lost,all trains shall coast as far as the momentum of the train and the signalling system permit, after ascertaining from Traffic Controller that there is no defectin the overhead contact wire or third rail system,as the case may be. The objective is to get every train to a platform or as close to the platform as possible where passengers can be detrained if the incident is likely to be prolonged;
